{
  "id": "mcq-remove-key-from-object",
  "unit": "concat-and-remove",
  "mode": "choice",
  "tier": "easy",
  "title": "Which script produces this output?",
  "topics": [
    "-",
    "--",
    "mapObject"
  ],
  "examObjective": "Applying correct syntax to write DataWeave transformations to coerce, format, order, and filter data",
  "prompt": "Given the payload below, **which script produces exactly this output?**\n\n```\n{ \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Ann\" }\n```",
  "inputMime": "application/json",
  "outputMime": "application/json",
  "choice": {
    "kind": "which-script",
    "payload": "{\"id\":1,\"ssn\":\"123\",\"name\":\"Ann\"}",
    "target": "{ \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Ann\" }",
    "answer": 1,
    "options": [
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload - \"123\"",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload - \"ssn\"",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter ($$ != \"ssn\")",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload -- [\"id\", \"ssn\"]"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [],
  "solution": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload - \"ssn\"",
  "explanation": {
    "approach": "On an Object, `-` removes a key by name. The wrong options remove too much, use an Array function on an Object, or name a value instead of a key.",
    "snippets": [
      {
        "label": "The answer",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload - \"ssn\"",
        "payload": "{\"id\":1,\"ssn\":\"123\",\"name\":\"Ann\"}",
        "expect": {
          "output": "{ \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Ann\" }"
        },
        "note": "The field goes, the rest keep their order."
      },
      {
        "label": "Removing by value does nothing",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload - \"123\"",
        "payload": "{\"id\":1,\"ssn\":\"123\",\"name\":\"Ann\"}",
        "expect": {
          "output": "{ \"id\": 1, \"ssn\": \"123\", \"name\": \"Ann\" }"
        },
        "note": "There is no key called \"123\"."
      },
      {
        "label": "filter is for arrays",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter ($$ != \"ssn\")",
        "payload": "{\"id\":1,\"ssn\":\"123\",\"name\":\"Ann\"}",
        "expect": {
          "error": true
        },
        "note": "The Object version is `filterObject`."
      },
      {
        "label": "The filterObject version",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filterObject ((v, k) -> not (k ~= \"ssn\"))",
        "payload": "{\"id\":1,\"ssn\":\"123\",\"name\":\"Ann\"}",
        "expect": {
          "output": "{ \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Ann\" }"
        },
        "note": "This works too, but the key has to be compared with `~=`: a key is not a String."
      }
    ]
  }
}
